raw_response:
 Yes, I understand that you want to know how to create a pop-up window on a website using HTML and CSS. Here are the steps to create a simple pop-up window:

1. Create a new HTML file and add a `<div>` element inside the `<body>` tag.
2. Add an ID to the `<div>` element, for example, "popup".
3. Add some CSS to style the pop-up window. For example:
```css
#popup {
  position: absolute;
  top: 50%;
  left: 50%;
  transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
  width: 300px;
  background-color: #f2f2f2;
  padding: 20px;
  border: 1px solid #888;
  text-align: center;
}
```
4. Add an event listener to the `<div>` element using JavaScript. For example:
```javascript
var popup = document.getElementById("popup");

document.getElementById("show").addEventListener("click", function() {
  popup.style.display = "block";
});
```
5. Add a button to the website using an `<button>` element, and give it an ID, for example, "show".
6. Add the following JavaScript code to the website to show the pop-up window when the button is clicked:
```javascript
var popup = document.getElementById("popup");

document.getElementById("show").addEventListener("click", function() {
  popup.style.display = "block";
});
```
7. Test the pop-up window by clicking on the button.

Note: This is a simple example and you can add more features to the pop-up window like closing it after some time, adding images, videos, etc.

